@startuml
title Current implemented authentication, session, and authorization model

entity users {
  * user_id : UUID <<PK>>
  --
  username : VARCHAR(32)
  email : VARCHAR(320)
  password_hash : VARCHAR(72)
  role : ADMIN | USER
}

entity sessions {
  * session_id : UUID <<PK>>
  --
  user_id : UUID <<FK>>
  refresh_token_hash : VARCHAR(128) <<unique, not null>>
  refresh_token_expires_at : TIMESTAMP
  installation_id : VARCHAR(255)
  client_platform : VARCHAR(16)
  client_name : VARCHAR(255)
  client_version : VARCHAR(64)
  last_seen_ip : VARCHAR(45)
  last_seen_user_agent : VARCHAR(512)
  last_authenticated_at : TIMESTAMP
  revoked_at : TIMESTAMP <<nullable>>
  revocation_reason : VARCHAR(32) <<nullable>>
}

users ||--o{ sessions : owns

note right of sessions
Current implemented security foundation:

POST /api/auth/login
  -> BCrypt verification
  -> persisted session allocation
  -> session-bound JWT

POST /api/auth/refresh
  -> validate persisted session
  -> rotate refresh-token hash
  -> issue new JWT

Authenticated requests:
  -> validate JWT
  -> validate persisted session
  -> establish server-authoritative user
  -> apply endpoint authorization

POST /api/auth/logout
  -> revoke current session

Access token lifetime: 1 day
Refresh expiry: 30 days sliding
Maximum active sessions: 5

Realtime transport authentication and delivery
remain deferred.
end note
@enduml
